  "id": "COMPOUND:18896 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (Z,Z)-5,11-Eicosadienoic Acid and Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target interactions involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This compound appears to act as a mediator, with (Z,Z)-5,11-Eicosadienoic Acid directly targeting the complex, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The evidence is consistent across three distinct pathways, each linking the fatty acid to the enzyme through different ligands. These ligands—2,4,6-Trihydroxy-3-(3,3-Dimethylallyl)Acetophenone, 2-amino-3-(1-methyl-1H-imidazol-5-yl)propanoic acid, and Tetracosanoic Acid—suggest a broader pharmacological profile, potentially involving diverse mechanisms of action. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for (Z,Z)-5,11-Eicosadienoic Acid in modulating Phosphodiesterase 6C activity through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
